{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Grounds","html":"<article id='sn1.54'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.54 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 1.54 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>6. Jarāvagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>6. Old Age </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Vatthusutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Grounds </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kiṁsu vatthu manussānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“What is the site for human beings? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁsūdha paramo sakhā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What is the best comrade here? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kiṁsu bhūtā upajīvanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>By what do the creatures who live off the earth </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ye pāṇā pathavissitā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>sustain their life?” </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Puttā vatthu manussānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Children are the site for human beings. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhariyā ca paramo sakhā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A wife is the best comrade. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vuṭṭhiṁ bhūtā upajīvanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The creatures who live off the earth </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ye pāṇā pathavissitā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>sustain their life by rain.” </span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
